After being disgusted with the immoral existance as a vampire, drinking 
blood off his freshly killed corpses, Mekkis the wizard looked for a way 
out.  He had heard of a certain amulet that he could use to pursuade the 
"gods" the allow him to shed his undead form and ascend to a higher plane.

Taking his ancestorial ring of slow digestion, the ring of polymorph he 
was loath to use (mutating into a different form , an uncursed scroll of 
genocide and two scrolls of identify, he ventured into the dungeons of 
doom in an attempt to find the amulet.

With his starting spells (resist poison, force bolt, light and create 
monster), he manage to stay poison resistant.  He had found that as he 
attacked monsters, he involantariy fedd on their lifeblood in an attempt 
to weaken them,  He managed to morally justify this as he had read that 
"The draining of life is considered to be primarily a non-physical 
                     effect".

He found a hobbit who gave him a +2 elven mithril coat, that he used 
extensively early on.  The mall gave him cash for his spellbooks and 
ring of polymorph, and an oil lamp.  He then ventured to minetown, 
stumbling on a spellbook of identify along the way.  He found no magic 
lamps, but had managed to enhance dagger to maximum (he was meleeing for 
the fact that mithril doesn't play well with spells), and spammed light 
enough to be able to cast identify (his main method of BUC identification).

He the completed sokoban with no problems, notably finding a ring of 
fire resistance, and in the sokoban zoo, there was a randomly generated 
bag of holding in addition to the one that was to be his reward.  Back 
in the mines, he reached minesend and got the luckstone (he also found 
hellfire lying around, and picked it up - Mekkis had an unhealthy habit 
of carrying around artifacts that he'd never use).  On his way up, he 
found that his scroll of genocide had been cursed by his attempts to get 
wishes and see invisible by quaffing from fountains (he got neither).  A 
black unicorn in minetown increased his luck, so then he excavated a few 
rooms to the west of minetown and sealed them off with pits, then 
started his own personal casino.

His payout consisted of holy water, silver dragon scale mail, Magicbane, 
helm of brilliance, master key of thievery, spellbook of remove curse, 
magic marker, and numerous iron balls and chains.  He made a fool of 
himself by being jerked by the balls as they fell into the pits, until 
he found a convenient boulder.

On dlvl11, a rash fountain quaffing caused his BoH to become cursed, so 
he dropped it and increased his poison resistance timer until he could 
enhance protection to skilled and cast remove curse.  The going was 
uneventful until he reached Grund's stronghold, where he found out that 
he COULD choke on all the lifeblood he was sucking out of the numerous 
monsters insisting on destroying him.  After having some tough moments 
with being hit numerous times while trying to regain his composure, he 
found a discarded ring of regenration and developed his "feedback-based 
hunger management system" (when unsatiated, put on =oSD and take off 
=oRegen, when satiated, take off =oSD, when "having a hard time getting 
it down", put on =oRegen), that generally kept him from choking.

Three thrones and two genocides later (genociding "nothing" - he didn't 
want to start a holocost), he wished for his first lot of healthstones. 
  The quests were pretty much a pushover, throwing a paralysis potion at 
The Dark One and finishing him off with acid stream and lightning.  He 
then set up a stash near the portal of the chaotic quest.

One Eye'd Sam had two pairs of gauntlets of dexterity, the first magic 
whistle, and some unholy water, so Mekkis used a combination of scrolls 
of earth, poisoned daggers, and stinking cloud to liberate them.

He continued downwards, clearing out the other branches, finding a 
spellbook of finger of death concealed in a statue, and using it on 
medusa, only to have pegasus spring up and get caught by the reflection.

The castle had the first hawaiian shirt, and the wand of wishing was 
(0:3), but was otherwise unexciting.  Most of Gehennium was a pushover, 
with the exception of Demogorgon, who gated in some of his friends, but 
magicbane, wands of fire, and a blessed +6 unicorn horn fixed him 
permenantly.

He found and marked the viabrating square, refreshed his spells (by 
casting them all in quick succession), and entered the tower.  Outside 
the wizard's lair, he blew 3 more wishes on healthstones and wrote some 
spare scrolls of charging (for use on himself).  One finger later, and 
the wizard was a corpse, then he levelported to the viabrating square, 
performed the archaic invocation,

His pet at the time, a purple worm, had a nice time chomping wraiths 
through the graveyard, and was level 43 before he chomped the priest, 
leaving Mekkis to pick up the amulet and run.  As he was climbing, he 
teleported away 3 summoning storms, wished for a cursed potion of gain 
level to bypass Dispater's lair, encountered the wizard once, then made 
it to the plane of earth.

The elemental planes were trivial, and Mekkis noted that even inside an 
air elemental, he was regenerating health faster than he was losing it. 
  On arriving on Astral, he asked Pallas what the RNG's opinion of which 
altar he should visit.  The RNG spoketh "center", so he dealt with the 
requisite "reception party" - in this case 2 arch-liches, and waded his 
way through the priests, angels, insects, player-monsters, and Famine, 
until he found himself at Path's high altar.  Thinking to himself "well, 
Anhur is an idiot, and it just proves how gullible these 'gods' are", he 
donned a helm of opposite alignment, slammed the amulet on the altar, 
and drummed his fingers while the invisible choir accompanying Path's 
rituals....

